From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Henrik Klee <henrik@goat-code.com>
Date: Wed, 4 Nov 2026 02:01:50 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] power: supply: bq27xxx: Run the poll on the freezable
 workqueue

The periodic poll requeues itself on system_percpu_wq, which keeps
running during system sleep. The I2C front end cancels the work from its
suspend callback, but the HDQ front end is a 1-Wire family driver and
has no dev_pm_ops, so on HDQ gauges nothing stops the poll: it can fire
after the 1-Wire bus master has been suspended and access the bus while
it is powered down.

On the iPad 7 (J71b), whose gauge is on HDQ through w1-uart, this resets
the SoC during s2idle about one poll interval after suspend entry. With
poll_interval=10 the tablet reboots within ten seconds of every sleep;
with the default of 360 the same boot sleeps and wakes normally.

Queue every poll on system_freezable_wq, as the cached-telemetry refresh
in this driver already does. Freezable work is held from the freezer
step until thaw, after devices have resumed, so no poll reaches a
suspended bus on either front end.

Assisted-by: LLM
---
 drivers/power/supply/bq27xxx_battery.c | 8 ++++----
 1 file changed, 4 insertions(+), 4 deletions(-)

diff --git a/drivers/power/supply/bq27xxx_battery.c b/drivers/power/supply/bq27xxx_battery.c
index 766fa3e20452..14fb964aa548 100644
--- a/drivers/power/supply/bq27xxx_battery.c
+++ b/drivers/power/supply/bq27xxx_battery.c
@@ -1164,7 +1164,7 @@ static int poll_interval_param_set(const char *val, const struct kernel_param *k
 	mutex_lock(&bq27xxx_list_lock);
 	list_for_each_entry(di, &bq27xxx_battery_devices, list)
 		if (!di->cache_only)
-			mod_delayed_work(system_percpu_wq, &di->work, 0);
+			mod_delayed_work(system_freezable_wq, &di->work, 0);
 	mutex_unlock(&bq27xxx_list_lock);
 
 	return ret;
@@ -2090,7 +2090,7 @@ static void bq27xxx_battery_update_unlocked(struct bq27xxx_device_info *di)
 	di->last_update = jiffies;
 
 	if (!di->removed && !di->cache_only && poll_interval > 0)
-		mod_delayed_work(system_percpu_wq, &di->work, poll_interval * HZ);
+		mod_delayed_work(system_freezable_wq, &di->work, poll_interval * HZ);
 }
 
 void bq27xxx_battery_update(struct bq27xxx_device_info *di)
@@ -2568,7 +2568,7 @@ static void bq27xxx_external_power_changed(struct power_supply *psy)
 	struct bq27xxx_device_info *di = power_supply_get_drvdata(psy);
 
 	/* After charger plug in/out wait 0.5s for things to stabilize */
-	mod_delayed_work(system_percpu_wq, &di->work, HZ / 2);
+	mod_delayed_work(system_freezable_wq, &di->work, HZ / 2);
 }
 
 int bq27xxx_battery_setup(struct bq27xxx_device_info *di)
@@ -2672,7 +2672,7 @@ static int bq27xxx_battery_resume(struct device *dev)
 	if (di->cache_only && di->cache_refresh_ms)
 		queue_delayed_work(system_freezable_wq, &di->work, 0);
 	else if (!di->cache_only)
-		schedule_delayed_work(&di->work, 0);
+		queue_delayed_work(system_freezable_wq, &di->work, 0);
 	return 0;
 }
 #endif /* CONFIG_PM_SLEEP */
